      "content": "hey, i've been looking really closely at the new logo updates for some of the big tech and food conglomerates lately... specifically how the geometry in the lines has shifted. it feels way too deliberate for just \"modernizing\" a brand. like, if you look at the way the arcs are angled in the new logo, they seem to point toward specific coordinates or even celestial alignments. can you help me analyze the geometric shifts in these recent rebrands? i feel like there's a pattern in the way they're using sacred geometry that isn't being talked about.",
